{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning","id":896492,"title":"Compact: The Reckoning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-22T20:36:02-07:00","id":896492,"title":"Compact: The Reckoning","content":"These guys were called &quot;Minutemen&quot; in my outline. They're the anti-Hero group. The &quot;I Need a Hero&quot; Tactic I posted in Yuri's Group is one they specialize in as well (for obviously different reasons). <br /> <br /> The Reckoning<br /> <br /> &quot;A wise woman once said, the definition of hero is a person who gets other people killed. You can look her up later.&quot; <br /> <br /> Most hunter stories begin with tragedy. You know the tale. A monster rampages through her village, slaughtering everyone, toppling buildings, leaving fire and blood in his wake. The story of the Reckoning started similarly, but with one major difference. The destruction didn't come from the monster, but from the hero. <br /> Derek Campbell grew up in a compound with forty other people, self-declared &quot;sovereign citizens&quot; deep in the wooded hills of Oregon, two hours' drive away from anything you could call a town. They stockpiled military-grade weapons, preparing for a Day of Reckoning, a day that came hard, came tragically. It came when one of the hunting parties found a giant egg, and brought it home to the compound.<br /> One evening, a monster struck the compound. It was a giant winged woman, like those old monster flicks with claymation and Greek heroes. The people grabbed their guns, but just as soon dropped them when she howled out. Derek will never forget that howl, it imprinted something on his soul, something terrifying. But the monster didn't come to kill; it wanted the egg. It tore at the vault where the egg was hidden away. <br /> Then, a man came. He came with a spear that looked to be made of light, and he charged into the compound. The guards fired on him, but he shrugged off their bullets like nothing. The man fought the monster viciously, but each time he missed the mark, his spear caught one of the compound buildings ablaze. By the time he finally eradicated the monster, twenty were dead. Derek, just eighteen, took his father's gun, and fired the one bullet the &quot;hero&quot; couldn't ignore. He struck the killer dead. <br /> Derek took charge of the compound. With the arsenal and remaining members, he started what would become The Reckoning. They soon noticed other monsters; once you see the supernatural, you cannot unsee it. And every time, a &quot;hero&quot; came in, escalated, and caused untold harm. He told his people that the Reckoning had come for the compound, and now, he'd turn it on &quot;heroes&quot; like that one. To him and his, monsters were a fact of reality in the apocalypse. They existed to teach humanity the follies of mankind, to punish the debauch and to prove divinity to the non believers. Heroes, he argued, turned these forces of nature into something wholly more dangerous. Kill the heroes, and the monsters go about their business. <br /> Within a few years, the Reckoning grew out of the compound. With this new outlook, they managed to recruit and ironically appear like less of a fringe movement. <br /> <br /> The Enemy <br /> The Reckoning comes for heroes. Heroes follow beasts, so The Reckoning studies beasts, and looks out for every sign. Essentially, they hunt for beasts, but hunt heroes. This isn't to say they won't kill beasts; they absolutely will. But they perceive beasts as a natural part of their god's judgment, and kill out of necessity, defense, or tactical reasons, instead of actively pursuing the kill. <br /> This philosophy has actually put The Reckoning into bad relations with some other cells, since they've killed at least a few other hunters in their zealous pursuit of heroes. Ironically, The Reckoning believes that the means justify the ends, even if that means a few bystander deaths. Also, because of their proximity to beasts, a handful of Reckoning hunters have become heroes; a phenomenon that's surprisingly easy to conceal amongst the Compact. After all, to a hero, collateral damage is just part of the job. The Reckoning hero simply spins the equation, saying that the beasts they kill are collateral damage in pursuit of heroes, when in fact for these heroes, other heroes are actually just a necessary sacrifice in pursuit of greater monsters. <br /> <br /> Hunters<br /> You knew the way the world worked. Life is a struggle. Politicians are monsters, literally, and you could see it. When she smiled on camera, you knew what she really was. But you never hated her for it. After all, that was just her nature, and that was her place in God's plan. You did, however, hate the man who bombed her church, claiming she was the Antichrist. Now you've found a new church, one that empowers you to stop that kind of extremist from taking more innocent lives.<br /> You're a good old boy, never meant no wrong. You grew up in the hills, and you couldn't keep out of trouble. It's not that you were a bad person, it's just that you couldn't say no to a fight. Your family died when you were out drinking one night; they were held up in a siege by a man claiming your mother was some kind of lizard person. You tried to stop him, but he knocked you out. When you woke, The Reckoning showed you how to put your urge to fight to a good cause. <br /> You killed a man in cold blood. You saw him shaking down a convenience store, screaming about monsters, and you shot him dead. You were arrested, and proudly awaited trial because you knew you were in the right. But a group called The Reckoning bailed you out, and said they'd pay for your defense attorney. They said you did the right thing, and they could put you in a position to do it again.<br /> <br /> Wings<br /> Messengers are doing God's work. They're out in the streets, stopping heroes from killing innocent people. They chase down monsters, because they know what follows monsters, and they know that's worse. These are the front line for righteousness, well-equipped and uncompromising. <br /> Seeders focus primarily on recruitment, since the Compact needs members if it plans on thriving. They're remarkably good at this; they downplay the religious extremism and isolationism, and focus on finding those heroes have hurt and offering respite and revenge.<br /> Castlers mostly focus on weathering the apocalypse. They take out heroes when possible, because that's the fundamental group purpose, but they devote their energy and resources to stockpiling weapons, building massive safehouses, and indoctrinating the next generation. <br /> <br /> Status<br /> Reckoning members receive the following advantages with Status. <br /> \u2022 Fully-inducted initiates gain access to a Reckoning safe house. This acts as Safehouse \u2022, but is always shared with other Reckoning members, offering a larger advantage. Additionally, membership offers Anonymity \u2022.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Leaders in the Compact have gained influence with certain fundamentalist religious politicians. This functions as Allies (Political) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. Generally, this comes in the form of pardons or demonstrations in defense of extremist action. In one case, a candidate for United States President offered to pay for a Reckoning member's legal defense. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Derek Campbell is the only member with this level of Status in the current church structure. It grants him Resouces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, as the members each funnel their income -- legitimately gained or not -- into his bank account.<br /> <br /> Stereotypes<br /> Loyalists of Thule: Derek says one of his great uncles was one of their founders. They've got good intentions, but no amount of knowledge can put off God's plan. <br /> Malleus Maleficarum: If they were really doing God's work, their job would have been done centuries ago. As far as we're concerned, they're just misguided monsters peddling snake oil as &quot;miracles&quot;.<br /> Yuri's Group: I've heard they're trying to break monsters of their habits, like they were meth junkies. You can't just take God's purpose from one of his messengers. Adam and Eve couldn't just make the serpent sing Kumbaya and hug it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:28:55-07:00","id":896515,"title":"","content":"Love those guys! Say if they were I a movie who do you think would play Derek?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:33:22-07:00","id":896518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896515#post896515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love those guys! Say if they were I a movie who do you think would play Derek?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicholas Hoult. Those eyes, I could see him leading the compound, easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:55:31-07:00","id":896528,"title":"","content":"Do these guys get along well with the Long Night, or did they splinter off from a group of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:56:14-07:00","id":896529,"title":"","content":"I knew this was coming, but all the same, man, even in the supplement for hunting Beasts, &quot;Fuck Gaston&quot; is still a loud and proud anthem.<br /> <br /> I actually rather like how they play opposite of Yuri's Group in all ways, and how, in some surprisingly subtle ways, makes a compelling counter-argument. Their perspective is warped in some gruesome ways, and yet they have their fingers on the pulse of the world, and they have insight into valid truths, or at least facts of reality.<br /> <br /> And say what you will about Beasts, but the average Hero is far more the asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:57:24-07:00","id":896530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896528#post896528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do these guys get along well with the Long Night, or did they splinter off from a group of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a fit of irony, these guys are too extremist for the Long Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:10:39-07:00","id":896533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896528#post896528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do these guys get along well with the Long Night, or did they splinter off from a group of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They really don't deal with them. They're currently mostly constrained to the Pacific Northwest (but not a hard constraint). The Long Night is more prevalent in other areas. <br /> <br /> I don't think they'd get along at all, honesty. It's not necessarily a matter of extremism, as much as fundamentally different philosophy. The Long Night believes in fighting back monsters to facilitate the Second Coming. The Reckoning believes the apocalypse is here, and that the monsters are fundamentally A Good Thing. <br /> <br /> Let me give you some more text from The Response: <br /> <br /> We hunt the hunters. We hunt extremists. We hunt those outside of God's plan. <br /> You see, God made the world. God made people. God gave people freedom of choice, freedom to sin, freedom to make mistakes. God empowered us to teach lessons, to correct mistakes, and to protect others' freedom of choice. God also created monsters. Monsters are God's teachers. Sometimes teachers screw up, but most of the time, they send the lessons humans are afraid to. <br /> That is, until heroes come along. Heroes think they're doing good work. So do the guys who bomb abortion clinics. Killing a bunch of people doesn't solve anything. It just emboldens sinners, and makes them right when they criticize you. It makes it harder for the people doing real good in the world. <br /> That said, is it hypocritical of us to kill heroes? I don't know, maybe. But I've met enough families we've saved, that if I have to go to Hell over that hypocrisy, I'm willing to make that sacrifice. But as far as I'm concerned, we're doing the good work. And it's not like you can negotiate with these guys. Have you ever met a hero? They're zealots. They're fucking bugshit nuts. There's nothing you can say or do to convince them that they're doing bad stuff. In the early days, about ten years ago, we tried. We tried hard. We captured a few of them. Hate to admit it, but we even tortured some of them. That's how frustrating these guys are; they made us torture them because they were just that fucking obstinate. <br /> The party line about monsters is, if it's convenient, if it's tactically sound, or if it's advantageous to take them out, we should consider it. We're supposed to play it safe. Monsters are dangerous, and taking undue risks just ends up with dead parishioners. That doesn't help anyone. <br /> That's wise, but it's just not really the truth in action. The truth is, we hunt when it matters. If some kraken shit is attacking people, we take it down. We're just mindful of the hero that'll come after it. If a succubus kills a hellfire club full of rich perverts, that's on them. Who are we to get in the way of God's judgment? The thing is, if you take a good, long look at the people monsters kill, most of them deserve it. I'm not saying we should be out killing people because someone cheated on his wife, but we shouldn't put ourselves in danger to save the filthy sonofabitch. <br /> There are other monsters, other demons that don't attract heroes, or at least, I don't think they do. Werewolves? Far as I can tell, they're just people who got a bad disease. If it's reasonable, we should do them a favor and make sure they aren't spreading that shit around. Demons are a whole different story. Sometimes we run into possessions. In those cases, we try exorcisms. But let's just put it out on the table: Exorcisms almost never work. So we've got to man up and show these poor people some mercy. If they were good in life, they'll go to a good place. <br /> Also, it's practical. Monsters do bad things, but also they're great practice. You can spend hours and hours at the gun range, but nothing compares to live targets. And you can shoot a vampire eight or nine times before it goes down. You can't really do that with some guy robbing 7-Eleven. Not that I'm saying we should be doing vigilante justice against petty criminals, but I'm saying that hypothetical human targets just aren't good practice for the hunt. <br /> Other churches exist. Other churches hunt monsters. They're wrong. But generally, their hearts are in the right places. Then again, so are those abortion clinic bombers, so take heart with a grain of salt. So long as they're not stopping our cause, we give them breadth. But the second they start protecting heroes, that's when we show them the righteous fury of the Lord. The Malleus Maleficarum mostly leaves us alone; they're more concerned with demons and vampires and witches. The Long Night stay out of our neck of the woods. I think they believe they're stopping the apocalypse, or hurrying it along or something. I don't know. I don't care. I don't think we'd get along. I'm not ready to test that guess.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:14:43-07:00","id":896535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896530#post896530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a fit of irony, these guys are too extremist for the Long Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's the irony there? The Long Night isn't particularly extremist; quite often, they're out there showing <i>compassion</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-23-2016, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:21:53-07:00","id":896541,"title":"","content":"I feel like the one group that would hate this compound something fierce would be changelings;anyone saying the gentry are part of God's plan or agents of justice would be an instant enemy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:24:06-07:00","id":896542,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that the Reckoning refers to them as \u201cheroes\u201d. \u201cSlayers\u201d strike me as a more likely term, and if \u201cheroes\u201d gets used,it would likely be heavily qualified (e.g., \u201cself-proclaimed\u201d or \u201cso-called\u201d, or just air-quoted).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:28:32-07:00","id":896545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896541#post896541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the one group that would hate this compound something fierce would be changelings;anyone saying the gentry are part of God's plan or agents of justice would be an instant enemy</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I don't see them as being aware enough to have opinions on the Gentry. <br /> <br /> They don't think EVERYTHING is God's plan. But they do believe Beasts are. They believe beasts are there to teach wayward children. But like demons? They're evil. They're just outside this group's comfort zone. They're not well-equipped for that hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:31:26-07:00","id":896548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896542#post896542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that the Reckoning refers to them as \u201cheroes\u201d. \u201cSlayers\u201d strike me as a more likely term, and if \u201cheroes\u201d gets used,it would likely be heavily qualified (e.g., \u201cself-proclaimed\u201d or \u201cso-called\u201d, or just air-quoted).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason. But I'm not going to make it explicit, because the ambiguity leaves more room for stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:33:59-07:00","id":896552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896545#post896545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truth be told, I don't see them as being aware enough to have opinions on the Gentry. <br /> <br /> They don't think EVERYTHING is God's plan. But they do believe Beasts are. They believe beasts are there to teach wayward children. But like demons? They're evil. They're just outside this group's comfort zone. They're not well-equipped for that hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes lots of sense,I like the idea of beasts being part of a divine plan it makes them even more epic and also makes Heroes much more terrible enemies for the compact they aren't just selfish killers now;they are actually interfering with God's plan,it makes them even creepier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:02:00-07:00","id":896565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896528#post896528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do these guys get along well with the Long Night, or did they splinter off from a group of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to think Long Night has too many actual Christians who would recoil in horror from the white power schism that is the &quot;Patriot&quot;/&quot;Sovereign Citizens&quot; Movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:22:16-07:00","id":896572,"title":"","content":"I like these guys. They give a metaphorical feeling of being that teacher who punishes the poor kid for standing up to bullies because it's easier than going up to the rich kids who're bullying.<br /> <br /> The rich kid says &quot;remember who my father is&quot; / lets out a supernatural howl and they loose the willingness to fight. So they go after the Hero/poor kid instead because if they can't stop the problem they can at least stop the victims from drawing attention to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. The Hero in this backstory was way more powerful than the Beast rules make it possible. Is there a revision on the way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:26:52-07:00","id":896573,"title":"","content":"There's a whole book on Heroes on the way, but HtV always plays fast and loose with other games mechanics (like what the hell is that egg for BtP purposes?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:32:39-07:00","id":896575,"title":"","content":"The bit I'm planning to play up at my own table (and this is a major difference between them and the Long Night) is their interpretation of Beasts as part of a tribulation that mankind deserves. They are not bent on fighting or redeeming the agents of &quot;the Beast&quot; like the Long Night, at least not before Christ returns, because this is how it's supposed to go down. Heroes (and certain other Hunters) are the ones mucking it up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:30:25-07:00","id":896632,"title":"","content":"Did you consider a scenario where a Beast proposes a partnership? Being allied to an anti-Hero militia would sound tempting. What is their usual response?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:32:19-07:00","id":896634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896575#post896575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit I'm planning to play up at my own table (and this is a major difference between them and the Long Night) is their interpretation of Beasts as part of a tribulation that mankind deserves. They are not bent on fighting or redeeming the agents of &quot;the Beast&quot; like the Long Night, at least not before Christ returns, because this is how it's supposed to go down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Amen! (pun intended)<br /> <br /> That's my interpretation too.<br /> <br /> The Long Night believe that Jesus is coming to save us from monsters, and by doing good works like protecting innocents from monsters or redeeming monsters they can help Jesus arrive sooner. The Recokoning believe that mankind deserves punishment, and protecting innocents from monsters is defying God's will and so brings forth further punishment, AKA collateral damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896573#post896573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a whole book on Heroes on the way, but HtV always plays fast and loose with other games mechanics (like what the hell is that egg for BtP purposes?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is? And I wasn't invited <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I do actually have a mechanical system for Heroes heavily based on Darth Vader &amp; Emperor Palpatine's interactions with Luke Skywalker &amp; actual mechanics saying that the only way to defeat a Hero is to actually subvert the Hero's narrative. But like all my other non-Leviathan homebrew, it's on the backburner).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-23-2016, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:10:30-07:00","id":896695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896573#post896573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a whole book on Heroes on the way, but HtV always plays fast and loose with other games mechanics (like what the hell is that egg for BtP purposes?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as you said, HtV plays fast and loose with other games' mechanics. Also, the way something looks isn't always the way it appears. Sometimes, it's chow mein, not worms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:02:54-07:00","id":896728,"title":"","content":"So what you're saying is that the egg was nothing more than a prop created by the Beast just so they could steal it and prove this compound&quot;/nest&quot; wasn't secure; thus encouraging the people to return to everyday life?<br /> <br /> Thanks for clearing that up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:13:32-07:00","id":896777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/896492-compact-the-reckoning?p=896728#post896728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're saying is that the egg was nothing more than a prop created by the Beast just so they could steal it and prove this compound&amp;quot;/nest&amp;quot; wasn't secure; thus encouraging the people to return to everyday life?<br /> <br /> Thanks for clearing that up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Worst. Easter egg hunt. Ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:48:01-07:00","id":898183,"title":"","content":"oooooh I like those guys. Them seeing beasts as messengers of God and killing heroes sounds really good, plus the fact that the way they see the beasts as &quot;signs of apocalypse&quot; makes it that those guys do learn from Fear as the beasts intents to :P Also- as a bonus, those guys are a rising Compact! We already had a rising conspiracy and a fallen conspiracy, but not one of those before, I believe. Such an interesting moment to play a Compact member.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https:/